  "narrative": "The new interaction and conditional-effect panel largely supports the stability of the four accepted large associations while identifying one small, statistically detectable but clinically trivial batch interaction. For lineage subtype, all interaction estimates are close to zero and below the practical clinical-significance scale: H25 SMARCA4/SMARCA2 estimate -0.028 [-0.076, 0.020]; H26 MSI/WRN -0.021 [-0.085, 0.042]; H27 TP53/USP7 -0.010 [-0.053, 0.033]; H28 KEAP1/NFE2L2 -0.012 [-0.057, 0.033]. I therefore reject these lineage-subtype interaction claims as meaningful subgroup modifications. This does not prove complete homogeneity, but it gives no support for the accepted effects being driven only by adenocarcinoma versus the complement.  The screen-batch_a interactions are also small. H52 KEAP1/NFE2L2 +0.021 [-0.031, 0.072], H53 TP53/USP7 -0.019 [-0.064, 0.027], and H55 MSI/WRN +0.048 [-0.020, 0.115] have point estimates far below the 10%-or-0.1-scale benchmark and confidence intervals centered near zero. H54 SMARCA4/SMARCA2 is different in that its interval excludes zero, signed estimate -0.051 [-0.095, -0.007], but the magnitude is still small: it corresponds to a modest, opposite-signed batch modification and is only about 6% of the main SMARCA4/SMARCA2 effect. With many subgroup tests, I interpret this as statistically detectable but not clinically meaningful heterogeneity, and I reject it as a meaningful interaction.  The co-mutation-restricted main effects are very informative. H56, the KEAP1-loss effect on NFE2L2 dependency among TP53-loss lines, is strongly positive, signed estimate +0.810 [0.763, 0.857]; because the signed direction is +1, this indicates much weaker NFE2L2 dependency in KEAP1-loss lines even when TP53 is lost. H57, the TP53-loss effect on USP7 dependency among KEAP1-loss lines, is also large, +0.794 [0.754, 0.834], supporting weaker USP7 dependency in TP53-loss lines within KEAP1-loss contexts. H58, the SMARCA4-loss effect on SMARCA2 dependency among TP53-loss lines, is strong, +0.773 [0.729, 0.817], consistent with stronger SMARCA2 dependency in SMARCA4-loss lines. These conditional effects are all far larger than the clinical benchmark and indicate that the accepted effects are not limited to lines lacking another major genetic state. They remain observational dataset-level associations, not causal effects.  The pathway-specificity check H47 rejects ARID1A loss as an alternative broad BAF-complex explanation for the SMARCA4/SMARCA2 association: signed estimate -0.017 [-0.057, 0.023]. Since ARID1A loss is not associated with SMARCA2 dependency of comparable magnitude, the accepted SMARCA4/SMARCA2 effect remains more specific to SMARCA4 loss than to generalized BAF loss.  Overall, this panel strengthens confidence in the accepted effects: no lineage interaction is clinically meaningful; batch effects are mostly negligible, with one small SMARCA4/SMARCA2 modification; co-mutation-restricted effects remain very large; and an ARID1A control does not reproduce the SMARCA2 effect. I therefore request independent validation for H10, the SMARCA4-loss association with stronger SMARCA2 dependency, because it is canonical, pathway-specific, and now supported by direct co-occurrence and specificity checks. This validation will not establish causality or generalizability, but it would materially strengthen the dataset-level evidence.",
  "research_notes": "Accepted broad dataset-level associations remain H13 KEAP1 loss -> weaker NFE2L2 dependency (independently validated), H7 TP53 loss -> weaker USP7 dependency, H8 MSI-high -> stronger WRN dependency, and H10 SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency. Accepted restricted robustness claims are H29-H32. New accepted conditional effects: H56 KEAP1 effect within TP53-loss, H57 TP53 effect within KEAP1-loss, and H58 SMARCA4 effect within TP53-loss; all signed estimates about +0.77 to +0.81, far above the practical benchmark. Rejected/closed interaction and specificity claims: lineage interactions H25-H28 all small; batch interactions H52-H53, H55 small and non-significant; H54 batch_a SMARCA4/SMARCA2 interaction statistically detectable but small and opposite-signed, not clinically meaningful; H47 ARID1A loss does not reproduce SMARCA2 association. Validation budget: 8 remaining before this request. Requested independent validation for H10 SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2 dependency because it is canonical, now supported by lineage null interaction, small batch modification, co-occurrence robustness, and ARID1A negative control. Remaining untested/deferred items include marker interactions H37-H40, screen ROC H59, sex/culture/serum interactions H60-H62, cross-specificity H63-H65, library-stratified main effects H44-H46, adenocarcinoma main effects H14-H16/H43, and broad pathway tests H66-H71. Next iteration should assess H10 validation, then use remaining analyses to broaden specificity and technical robustness rather than over-validating highly similar canonical effects.",
